id: whack
name: Whack
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 10
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
exploitable: All adjacent Opponents.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A stack of Tension: a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge) at an Opponent below Injured, not at Long Range - won, a 1d10; on a 10, Defeated.
text: >
  Whack [1/Round]: In a risky gambit of a move, you attempt to eliminate your opponent, leaving them downed in a single blow if successful.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: 10(T)
  –Exploitable: All adjacent Opponents.
  –Effect: Spend a stack of Tension to target an Opponent who is not at Long Range and is below the Injured Health Threshold. Make a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge) against that Opponent. If you win, roll a 1d10. If you roll a 10, their Life Points are set to their lowest possible value and they are Defeated.

  You can only target each Opponent once per Combat Encounter with this Special Maneuver.

---

# A Special Maneuver: open where an effect grants it - the Priest Vocation. Used, which Opponent asked - Injured or
# Critical, not at Long Range, not Whacked before this Encounter - a stack of Tension (Battle Tension's) spent, and the Clash
# opened; won, the 1d10 rolled on its card - a 10, their Life Points at their lowest (chat.mjs whack, settleWhack).
[on used]
whack();
